    "prompt": "Below is a description of the Python function `StylesBuilder._process_fractional`.\n\nDescription:\n\"\"\"\nThe `_process_fractional` function is a method within the `StylesBuilder` class, designed to process a specific type of CSS property related to fractional values. It takes two parameters: `name`, a string representing the name of the CSS property, and `tokens`, a list of `Token` objects that contain the parsed values of the property. The function's primary purpose is to validate and convert these tokens into a float value suitable for setting a CSS rule, specifically for properties like opacity that can be expressed as percentages or decimal numbers.\n\nThe function begins by checking if the `tokens` list is empty. If it is, the function immediately returns without making any changes, effectively handling an early exit condition for empty input. It then examines the first token in the list. If there is more than one token, it sets an `error` flag to `True` because the function is designed to handle only single-token inputs.\n\nIf the token is valid and represents a scalar value ending with a percentage sign, the function attempts to convert this percentage string into a float using the `percentage_string_to_float` helper function. If successful, it sets the corresponding CSS rule using the `set_rule` method of the `self.styles` object, converting the property name from a hyphenated format to an underscored format for consistency. If the conversion fails due to a `ValueError`, the `error` flag is set to `True`.\n\nSimilarly, if the token represents a number, the function attempts to convert it to a float and clamp it between 0 and 1 using the `clamp` function. If successful, it sets the CSS rule. If the conversion fails, the `error` flag is again set to `True`.\n\nIf any of these conditions fail, indicating an invalid token or conversion error, the function calls the `error` method of the `self.styles` object, passing the property name, the problematic token, and a help text generated by the `fractional_property_help_text` function. This method is responsible for logging or reporting the error, providing context and guidance for correcting the issue.\n\nIn summary, the `_process_fractional` function is a utility for processing and validating fractional CSS properties, ensuring that they are correctly converted and applied to the styles, while also handling errors gracefully by reporting them with helpful information.\n\"\"\"\n\nSplit the description into atomic claims. Each claim must be a single, self-contained factual statement about the function that could be checked against the function's source code (name the function explicitly; no pronouns referring to other claims). Do not add claims that are not in the description; do not merge two facts into one claim. Keep the original wording where possible. Assign each claim exactly one type:\n- \"structural\": the function's signature, parameter names/defaults/types, return type, or which functions, methods, classes or attributes it uses.\n- \"dataflow\": how a value is computed, transformed, passed on, or what is returned for which input.\n- \"behavioural\": exceptions raised or caught, conditions/early returns, side effects, edge-case handling, ordering/iteration behaviour.\n- \"intent\": purpose, rationale, or the role of the function in the larger system.\n\nReturn a JSON array of at most 12 objects: [{\"text\": \"...\", \"type\": \"structural|dataflow|behavioural|intent\"}, ...]",
